course: dictionary
lesson: 13756
title: Words that mix together
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe things joining together. Intermingle means to mix together, so that the different parts are spread among each other. Clues in the sentence show you the meaning. «The blue and yellow paint intermingled and turned green» tells you the two colours mixed so well that they made a new colour.
explain: The word also describes people. When people intermingle, they mix and mingle in a group, talking with people they did not come with. «At the party, the children intermingled with the grown-ups.» Nobody stayed in their own corner: everyone was talking to everyone.
explain: Look for the small words that often come after it: intermingle with, or intermingled with. «The old songs intermingled with new rhythms» means the two styles were mixed up together. Try swapping in mix together: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Intermingle means to mix together, so the parts are spread among each other.
fact: «Intermingle» can describe things, such as smells, colours and liquids, or people in a crowd.
fact: «The smell of baking intermingled with the smell of rain.» Two smells mixed together in the air.
fact: When peoples and cultures intermingle, they share foods, words and customs.
fact: Phrases to watch for: intermingle with and intermingled with.
exercise: «The red and white paint intermingled on the paper.» What does intermingled mean? | Split into two piles | Thrown away | *Mixed together | Dried quickly
exercise: «At the party, the shy boy intermingled with the other guests.» What does intermingled with suggest? | Left the party early | Ate all the cake alone | Hid under the table | *Mixed and talked with people he did not come with
exercise: «The sweet and sour smells intermingled in the kitchen.» Find and copy the word that means mixed together. | sweet | kitchen | smells | *intermingled
test: «Traders from many lands intermingled in the old port.» What is the best meaning of intermingled? | Stayed far apart | Argued loudly | Sailed away | *Mixed together
test: Ella says intermingle is just another word for sit. Why is she wrong? | It means to sit down in a row | *It means to mix together, not to sit | It means to shout | It means to fall asleep
exam: Which sentence shows things mixing so that their parts are spread among each other? | The two rivers froze solid | The two rivers stayed separate, one blue and one brown | *The two rivers intermingled, and their waters swirled together | The two rivers ran uphill
